{"id":"wild-atlantic-way-bike","title":"Wild Atlantic Way by bike: Galway to Kinsale","who":"Classic route · Ireland's west coast","when":"May to September","vehicle":"Touring bike, about 2 weeks","kind":"bike","color":"#15803d","summary":"The southern half of the world's longest defined coastal route: Connemara's bogs and mountains, the Cliffs of Moher and the Burren, the Dingle peninsula and Slea Head, the Ring of Kerry and Beara, ending in the food town of Kinsale. Wind, rain, pubs and music; 80–100 km a day.","sources":[{"label":"Cycloscope: Ireland, the Wild Atlantic Way by bicycle","url":"https://cycloscope.net/cycling-ireland-wild-atlantic-way-bicycle/"},{"label":"Discover Ireland: cycling the Wild Atlantic Way","url":"https://www.discoverireland.ie/wild-atlantic-way/wild-atlantic-way-cycle"}],"approximate":"Main stops; the line follows quiet roads near the coast.","km":649,"bbox":[-10.2893,51.6773,-8.518,53.4884],"stops":[{"name":"Galway","place":"Galway, Ireland","at":[53.2744,-9.0491],"text":"A lively harbour city of music pubs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Galway_cathedral.jpg/500px-Galway_cathedral.jpg","page":"Galway","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galway_cathedral.jpg","credit":"Unknown authorUnknown author","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Clifden","place":"Clifden, Ireland","at":[53.4885,-10.0211],"text":"Into Connemara: lakes, bog and the Twelve Bens, about 94 km.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/ClifdenOverview.JPG/500px-ClifdenOverview.JPG","page":"Clifden","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ClifdenOverview.JPG","credit":"Bert Kaufmann","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Doolin","place":"Doolin, Ireland","at":[53.0163,-9.3776],"text":"Back through Galway and the Burren's limestone to the Cliffs of Moher.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Cliffs-Of-Moher-OBriens-From-South.JPG/500px-Cliffs-Of-Moher-OBriens-From-South.JPG","page":"Cliffs of Moher","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cliffs-Of-Moher-OBriens-From-South.JPG","credit":"Bjørn Christian Tørrissen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Kilrush","place":"Kilrush, County Clare","at":[52.6397,-9.4836],"text":"Out to Loop Head, then the ferry over the Shannon.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Irl_Loop_Head_LH.jpg/500px-Irl_Loop_Head_LH.jpg","page":"Loop Head","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Irl_Loop_Head_LH.jpg","credit":"Charles W Glynn","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Dingle","place":"Dingle, Ireland","at":[52.1415,-10.2895],"text":"Slea Head and the Blasket Islands from the end of Europe.","source":{"label":"Cycloscope","url":"https://cycloscope.net/cycling-ireland-wild-atlantic-way-bicycle/"}},{"name":"Kenmare","place":"Kenmare, Ireland","at":[51.8791,-9.584],"text":"Round the Ring of Kerry, or over the passes of the Iveragh peninsula.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Atlantic_Ocean%2C_Ring_of_Kerry_%28506559%29_%2827964189752%29.jpg/500px-Atlantic_Ocean%2C_Ring_of_Kerry_%28506559%29_%2827964189752%29.jpg","page":"Ring of Kerry","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantic_Ocean%2C_Ring_of_Kerry_%28506559%29_%2827964189752%29.jpg","credit":"Robert Linsdell from St. Andrews, Canada","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Bantry","place":"Bantry, Ireland","at":[51.6798,-9.4524],"text":"The Healy Pass over the Beara peninsula."},{"name":"Kinsale","place":"Kinsale, Ireland","at":[51.7057,-8.523],"text":"Along West Cork's coves to a harbour town famous for seafood.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Kinsale_%284693044621%29.jpg/500px-Kinsale_%284693044621%29.jpg","page":"Kinsale","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinsale_%284693044621%29.jpg","credit":"Christopher Michel","license":"CC BY 2.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"